        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(scripts): preserve surrogate pairs when truncating LLM text in bench dump",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`scripts/repro/tool-surface-live-bench.ts` uses `String.prototype.slice(0, N)` at three sites to truncate LLM output text for benchmark trail/log output. `slice` operates on UTF-16 code units, so when a surrogate pair (emoji, CJK character) straddles the cut boundary at position 299-300 or 399-400, the result contains an unpaired high surrogate — invalid Unicode that downstream consumers may reject.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReplace with `truncateUtf16Safe` from `@openclaw/normalization-core/utf16-slice`, the same helper already used across the codebase for safe UTF-16 boundary truncation. Sibling UTF-16 PRs (#104054, #107664, #109561, #109498, #109839) all use the same helper. The 300- and 400-code-unit limits and all non-truncated output remain unchanged.\n\nCollision check: searched open PRs for `tool-surface-live-bench`, `truncateUtf16Safe`, `bench dump`; no same-file or same-problem open PR was found.\n\n## User Impact\n\nBenchmark trail and result dump output no longer produces invalid Unicode. No production impact — this file is a `scripts/repro/` bench tool.\n\n## Evidence\n\nI ran the same throwaway TypeScript probe against the real imported `truncateUtf16Safe` helper with boundary-straddling `🐱` (U+1F431) input at the same lengths used by the bench script's three truncation sites (300 for ASSISTANT text, 400 for TOOLRESULT and finalText).\n\nBefore the fix, with the three production truncation lines restored to `.slice(0, N)`:\n\n```\n{\"fix\":\"before (raw .slice)\",\"ASSISTANT_text_unpaired\":true,\"TOOLRESULT_unpaired\":true,\"finalText_unpaired\":true,\"assist_length\":300,\"tool_length\":400,\"final_length\":400}\n```\n\nAfter the fix:\n\n```\n{\"fix\":\"after (truncateUtf16Safe)\",\"ASSISTANT_text_unpaired\":false,\"TOOLRESULT_unpaired\":false,\"finalText_unpaired\":false,\"assist_length\":299,\"tool_length\":399,\"final_length\":399}\n```\n\nFocused regression suite after rebasing onto current `upstream/main`:\n\n```\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs test/scripts/tool-surface-live-bench.test.ts\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\nTests  8 passed (8)\n```\n\nTargeted `oxfmt --check` and `git diff --check` passed. I did not run a live multi-provider LLM bench, but the probe exercises the exact same production import, boundary lengths, and format strings used by the bench script's three truncation sites and verifies no trailing high surrogates at any site.",
